Docs only; the survey is complete for its stated scope and every process was stopped by explicit PID.

THE DELIVERABLE. Running the hazard command in full in a clean worktree leaves 41 tracked files
modified (the hazard commit counted 39; composition matches). §3.3b of the report is the mapping:
28 of the 41 carry an exact responsible test file, merged from the whole-suite run's per-worker
audit-hook shards and the per-batch attribution runs. The 13 unattributed are the subprocess class
(a CPython audit hook cannot see a child process — Vivado, yosys) plus a tail the last xdist worker
had not flushed when the survey was stopped.

Two entries deserve attention on their own:
  * results/experiment_410_precision_live.json is written by test_experiment_431_eorm_jepa_retrain.py
    — a test for a DIFFERENT experiment. Any repair or audit that pairs test_experiment_N with
    experiment_N by name misses it entirely.
  * openspec/papers/paper-v6/section-6-limitations.md — a PAPER section — is written by
    test_experiment_1911.py.

RECORD INTEGRITY. All 31,564 tracked files hashed at session start and again after every survey
process was stopped. Exactly 12 differ and all 12 are this session's deliberate edits; no results/,
output/ or operator-curated public doc changed, and determination_preservation_lint --all is clean
across every tracked results/**/*.json. Nine artifacts were rewritten during the investigation
(dogfooding, reproductions, leaks) and every one was restored and proven byte-identical by sha256.

AND THE VERIFICATION ITSELF HAD THE BUG THE SESSION IS ABOUT. The first run of that comparison
printed "NONE — the research record is byte-identical" and had verified nothing: the
diff | grep '^>' | awk chain read $2 (the sha256 hash) where the path is $3, because the "> " prefix
shifts the fields, so it grepped hashes for ^results/ and matched nothing. It was caught only
because a file this session HAD edited was missing from the output. Recorded in §5 rather than
quietly fixed — a check that runs, passes, and inspects the wrong thing is precisely the failure
mode this whole session is about, and "the verification passed" is exactly the claim a reader
cannot otherwise audit.

